export anchor DiplomaStyle:
    number: 124
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Diploma
    idea: The dashboard as a formal certificate on parchment, with a double gilt frame, wax seals for the numbers, a numbered register of projects and a signature line under every activity.
    base: light
    palette:
        parchment: #f3ead2, the page behind the certificate
        sheet: #fbf5e4, the certificate, fields and the style sheet
        ink: #2a2118, text, the 2px frame, rules and bar outlines
        sepia: #5c4a33, meta lines, captions and nav links
        gilt: #b8963f, frame hairlines, corner ornaments and the focus halo, never text
        goldInk: #6b5317, roman numerals, the kicker and progress fill
        sealWax: #ead9a2, the four summary seals
        oxblood: #7d1f1f, the primary button, overdue, the Behind square and the big seal
        laurel: #2e5a35, the On track round seal
        amber: #7a4a00, the At risk diamond
    type:
        Text uses Palatino Linotype, Palatino, Book Antiqua, URW Palladio L,
        Georgia, serif. Signatures use Snell Roundhand, Apple Chancery, URW
        Chancery L, Lucida Calligraphy, cursive. The greeting is 64px italic
        at 1.1, section titles 26px small caps tracked 0.14em and centred,
        project names 22px italic 600, seal numbers 40px 600, body 17px at
        1.6, meta 15px small caps, signatures 22px script.
    layout:
        One centred certificate up to 1200px wide with a 2px ink border, a
        gilt double hairline inside and curled gilt ornaments in each corner.
        The masthead has a shield mark and the spaced small caps brand on the
        left, then an underlined italic search, an oxblood New project button
        with an inset gold line, a round bell and a monogram seal with the
        name. The nav is one centred row of small caps links split by gilt
        bullets, Home bold and underlined in oxblood. A centred proclamation
        follows with the kicker Brightwork hereby greets, the big italic
        greeting, the date written as Saturday, the 31st of October 2026, and
        Be it noted that 4 tasks are overdue between two rules. Four scalloped
        wax seals hold the numbers with small caps captions, the overdue seal
        in pink and oxblood. The Register of Projects is a list ruled with
        triple lines, each row a roman numeral, an italic name over team and
        due date, a dotted leader from percent to tasks above a thin framed
        bar, and the status on the right. Below sit two columns, a framed
        hatched bar chart titled Record of Tasks Completed, and Attestations,
        where each activity sentence sits over a signature rule with the name
        in script and the time in small caps. Two signature lines and a round
        oxblood star seal close the page. Below 900px seals go two by two and
        rows stack, below 560px the masthead centres and the sign-off stacks.
    spacing: An 8px unit. Rows have 16px padding, seals 24px gaps and sections 48px between them.
    density: Ceremonial and centred. One register of six rows, then a chart and six attestations side by side.
    corners: Square everywhere. Only seals, the monogram and the bell are round.
    borders: A 2px ink frame with gilt hairlines inside, triple ruled register ends, dotted leaders and signature rules.
    shadows: None. Inset double lines on buttons and frames stand in for depth.
    icons:
        Filled seal-like status marks at 18px with the small caps word, a
        round seal with a check for On track, a diamond with a bar for At
        risk and a square with a cross for Behind. Tools use thin 1.4 stroke
        line icons.
    focus: A 2px oxblood outline offset 3px inside a 6px soft gilt halo. A focused field gets a pale gold fill and a 2px oxblood underline.
    tone: Formal and ceremonial, such as Brightwork hereby greets and Be it noted that 4 tasks are overdue.
